course: dictionary
lesson: 12847
title: Words of endearment
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: An endearment is a loving word or name you call someone. «Night night, sweetheart» tells you the speaker cares about the person, so sweetheart is an endearment. Other examples are «darling», «love» and «pet».
explain: Context gives you the clues. Who is speaking, how they say it, and what is happening all help. A gran saying «Come on, pet» to her grandchild is showing love. She does not mean the child is an animal, even though a pet is usually an animal.
explain: Endearment can also mean the act of showing love or affection. When a couple give each other a hug and a soft word, the word and the hug are both endearments. Try swapping in a different meaning: if it still makes sense, you have understood the word.
fact: An endearment is a loving word or name you call someone.
fact: Endearment can also mean the act of showing love or affection.
fact: «Love», «sweetheart», «darling» and «pet» are all endearments.
fact: «Love» is common in northern England, «pet» in north-east England, «hen» in Scotland and «darl» in Australia.
fact: Endearments are often used by parents, grandparents and couples to show they care.
exercise: In «Night night, sweetheart», what kind of word is sweetheart? | A type of sweet cake | A word for a bad mood | The name of a street | *A loving name you call someone
exercise: Ella's gran in Newcastle says «Ta-ra, pet». What is pet doing here? | Telling Ella to go away | A cat or dog is being named | Asking for money | *Showing love and affection
exercise: Which word is a term of endearment? | *Darling | Table | Quickly | Window
test: «Hen», said by a Scottish nan to her grandchild, is what kind of word? | *An endearment | A place name | A type of bird | A word for a meal
test: Which sentence shows endearment as an act of affection? | *She called him darling and gave him a tight hug | They walked to school together | The bus was late again | She read the map carefully
exam: Why do families use words like «sweetheart» with each other? | *To show love and care | To sell food | To count how many words they know | To make people shout
